WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.535
-Progressives in Congress,

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:04.737
including Senate Budget
Chairman Bernie Sanders,

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:07.440
are pushing forward
with the transformative

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.509
$3.5 trillion spending plan

00:00:09.509 --> 00:00:12.044
that would invest heavily
in climate infrastructure

00:00:12.044 --> 00:00:14.013
and historic wildfires,
droughts, and flooding

00:00:14.013 --> 00:00:17.083
and, now, centrists with ties
to the fossil fuel industry

00:00:17.083 --> 00:00:18.284
are trying to water it down.

00:00:18.284 --> 00:00:20.520
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.590
♪♪

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.492
If you've been living pretty
much anywhere in the U.S.,

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:28.962
I don't have to tell you that
the effects of climate change

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.796
are here, and they are real.

00:00:30.796 --> 00:00:31.998
You can see it everywhere,

00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:34.667
from wildfires and droughts
across the West

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.536
to intense storms in the Gulf,

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:38.604
to flooding in New York City.

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:40.439
-The Bootleg Fire
in southern Oregon

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:42.942 line:0%
scorching more
than 280,000 acres.

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:44.610 line:0%
-Dozens of western wildfires

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:45.879 line:0%
burning out of control,

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:48.647 line:0%
sending smoke as far east
as New York City.

00:00:48.647 --> 00:00:50.283 line:0%
-Record-setting
low temperatures.

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:51.350 line:0%
Lots of areas,

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:52.418 line:0%
particularly across the South,

00:00:52.418 --> 00:00:53.853 line:0%
not used to serious
winter weather

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.922 line:0%
getting absolutely buried
under snow.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.690 line:0%
-The remnants of Hurricane Ida

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.959 line:0%
dumped billions
of gallons of water

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:02.161 line:0%
with stunning speed
on communities

00:01:02.161 --> 00:01:03.663 line:0%
from New York to Maryland.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.297 line:0%
-The National Weather Service
in New York City,

00:01:05.297 --> 00:01:07.233 line:0%
for the first time
in its history,

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.468 line:0%
issuing a flash flood emergency.

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:10.603 line:0%
-In Central Park,

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.938 line:0%
5.2 inches of water fell

00:01:12.938 --> 00:01:14.473 line:0%
in just three hours,

00:01:14.473 --> 00:01:18.177 line:0%
a 1-in-500-year rainfall event.

00:01:18.177 --> 00:01:20.980 line:0%
-They're calling it
a once-in-every-500-year

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:22.982 line:0%
flood here in Philadelphia.

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:24.217 line:0%
-And, in addition
to the flooding,

00:01:24.217 --> 00:01:26.052 line:0%
people in Pennsylvania
and New Jersey

00:01:26.052 --> 00:01:28.454 line:0%
are also cleaning up
after tornadoes.

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:31.023
-New Jersey tornados.

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:33.926
New Jersey Tornado sounds like
an Arena Football League team.

00:01:33.926 --> 00:01:35.060
The New Jersey tornadoes

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.829
left a wake of destruction
in their path,

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:37.997
but it could've been
a lot worse,

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:40.666
if they hadn't been stuck
in turnpike traffic.

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:42.034
[ Jersey accent ]
Hey, let's go!

00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:44.437
Some of us got trees to uproot.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:45.738
Don't get in the E-ZPass Lane

00:01:45.738 --> 00:01:47.607
if you don't have E-ZPass,
Grandma.

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.541
Just for the record,
I would 100%

00:01:49.541 --> 00:01:52.111
watch a Jersey-based remake
of the movie "Twister,"

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:55.481
starring Little Steven
and Marisa Tomei.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:56.582
[ As Little Steven ]
You're not gonna
freakin' believe this,

00:01:56.582 --> 00:01:58.050
but a cow just flew by.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.785
[ As Tomei ] You think I didn't
see the freaking cow, you moron?

00:01:59.785 --> 00:02:00.886
[Bleep] outta here.

00:02:00.886 --> 00:02:03.122
[ Laughter ]
And...

00:02:03.122 --> 00:02:04.557
...you knew it was
a New Jersey tornado

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.392
because it was
in a velour tracksuit,

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:09.095
shaking down a restaurant owner
for protection money.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.663
[ Jersey accent ]
You don't have my money?
Maybe my friend, here,

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:13.132
blows your pockets inside out.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:14.367
And those are jokes...

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.835
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:17.503
...about New Jersey tornadoes.

00:02:17.503 --> 00:02:20.573
Also, the rainfall in New York
was a once-in-a-500-year event.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:21.807
Think about how crazy that is.

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:24.611
It used to be that
a once-in-a-500-year event

00:02:24.611 --> 00:02:26.479
was the F Train arriving on time

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.814
or the Jets
starting a season 2 and 0.

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:30.350
[ Laughter ]
It's not an exaggeration to say

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.518
that the unprecedented
New York City floods

00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:34.520
essentially shut down parts

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.455
of the country's largest
transportation system.

00:02:36.455 --> 00:02:37.657
I mean, look at this.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.192
-We also have shots
of our subway system here

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:40.293
in New York City

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:42.361 line:0%
inundated with water,
flooding there.

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:43.762 line:0%
You can see it.

00:02:43.762 --> 00:02:45.097 line:0%
The entire subway service,

00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:46.832 line:0%
all over the city
of New York City,

00:02:46.832 --> 00:02:49.902 line:0%
suspended because of the
weather from Ida,

00:02:49.902 --> 00:02:52.371 line:0%
which includes, obviously,
rain, flooding.

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:53.472 line:0%
Look at that.

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:54.874 line:0%
See at the very back of that?

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:56.876 line:0%
Look how that water
is just pouring

00:02:56.876 --> 00:02:58.278 line:0%
into the New York City subway.

00:02:58.278 --> 00:03:00.179 line:0%
So the entire New York City
subway system

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:02.849 line:0%
out of commission right now.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.984
-The flooding was so bad,
they replaced the trains

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:06.752
with kayaks and, even then,

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:08.520
there was a guy
hugging the pole.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.123
[ Laughter ]
Nothing worse than getting
on a kayak at West 4th

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:12.425
and then, you get to 14th

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.893
and a mariachi band gets on
and tips the whole thing.

00:03:14.893 --> 00:03:16.896
I mean, look at that.
It looks like a Class 5

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.631
white water rapid or, I guess,

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.700
a brown water rapid?

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:22.869
Anyway, the point is
climate change is causing

00:03:22.869 --> 00:03:25.137
all kinds of extreme weather
events across the country.

00:03:25.137 --> 00:03:26.172
In the last few months, alone,

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:28.040
New York City has seen
deadly flooding,

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.209
record rainfall,
and wildfire smoke drifting

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:32.144
all the way from the West,
that turned the sun red

00:03:32.144 --> 00:03:33.846
and made the air unhealthy
to breathe.

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:35.014
And it may seem
counterintuitive,

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:36.583
but scientists are also
investigating

00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.451
the possibility
that climate change

00:03:38.451 --> 00:03:41.153
may have made the record
low temperatures in Texas

00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:44.289
that caused power outages
over the winter much worse.

00:03:44.289 --> 00:03:46.492 line:0%
Studies have already found
that Arctic warming

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:49.862 line:0%
may be driving some winter
extremes in lower latitudes

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.464 line:0%
and pushing cold air
over parts of the U.S.

00:03:52.464 --> 00:03:54.000 line:0%
And The New York Times
reported that...

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:10.616
And I personally think that's
a much more appropriate phrase

00:04:10.616 --> 00:04:12.618
because, in addition
to wreaking havoc,

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:14.286
making the planet uninhabitable,

00:04:14.286 --> 00:04:17.422
climate change is also
making things much weirder.

00:04:17.422 --> 00:04:18.858
Now, it's just normal

00:04:18.858 --> 00:04:21.027
for friends to show up to dinner
in late September

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:22.395
looking like they just
ran a marathon.

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:24.130
Pretty soon, the traditional

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.831
Thanksgiving feast
is going to be replaced

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:28.300
by a clothing-optional
backyard barbecue.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:29.669
"It's too hot for turkeys,

00:04:29.669 --> 00:04:31.704
so we're just doing
mashed-potato smoothies."

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.806
[ Laughter ]
This is how bad
climate change is getting --

00:04:33.806 --> 00:04:35.407
wildfires in the West,
floods in the East,

00:04:35.407 --> 00:04:37.410
freezing cold in Texas.
Billy Joel's going to have

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.579
to write an update for 2021
and call it...

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.616
What's that?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.616 --> 00:04:45.351
You want me to try and do one?
Oh, okay.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:47.086
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.086 --> 00:04:48.420
♪ Wildfires, power's down ♪

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:49.789
♪ Mare's back in "Easttown" ♪

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:51.057
♪ Bill Gates divorce ♪

00:04:51.057 --> 00:04:52.324
♪ Derby's got a doped-up horse ♪

00:04:52.324 --> 00:04:53.592
♪ Tracks flooding, toxic air ♪

00:04:53.592 --> 00:04:54.994
♪ Biden falling up the stairs ♪

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:56.262
♪ Hurricane, tornadoes ♪

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:58.397
♪ Emmy gold for "Ted Lasso" ♪

00:04:58.397 --> 00:05:00.332
[ Laughter ]
What?

00:05:00.332 --> 00:05:02.334
You want to do a second verse?!

00:05:02.334 --> 00:05:04.637
[ Laughter ]
You think? Okay.

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:06.105
♪ Pfizer versus J&amp;J ♪

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:07.406
♪ Gavin Newsom's A-okay ♪

00:05:07.406 --> 00:05:08.775
♪ Nicki's cousin's
friend's sack ♪

00:05:08.775 --> 00:05:09.975
♪ Jean Smart's comeback ♪

00:05:09.975 --> 00:05:11.210
♪ Brady had a big win ♪

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.645
♪ Rudy married his cousin ♪

00:05:12.645 --> 00:05:13.846
♪ Rioters at the door ♪

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:15.380
♪ I can't take it anymore ♪

00:05:15.380 --> 00:05:16.582
Thank you.

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:19.452
[ Laughter ]
Say what you will.

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:21.287
That's not a worse song
than the original.

00:05:21.287 --> 00:05:22.655
[ Laughter ]

00:05:22.655 --> 00:05:24.089
And, on top of floods
and hurricanes

00:05:24.089 --> 00:05:25.358
and wildfires
and everything else,

00:05:25.358 --> 00:05:26.793 line:0%
we're also seeing
the devastating effect

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:28.661 line:0%
on wildlife
and natural ecosystems.

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:30.162
In July,
the New York Times reported

00:05:30.162 --> 00:05:31.697
that the Western heat wave

00:05:31.697 --> 00:05:33.900
killed marine wildlife
in large numbers...

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:46.045
One marine biologist
told The Times...

00:05:49.649 --> 00:05:50.849
And it does.

00:05:50.849 --> 00:05:52.518
In fact, I tried to sell
Hollywood Studios

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:54.187
a screenplay for a movie
with that exact plot.

00:05:54.187 --> 00:05:55.722 line:0%
It was called...

00:05:55.722 --> 00:05:57.155 line:0%
It took place
in a dystopian future

00:05:57.155 --> 00:05:58.257 line:0%
where a marine biologist,

00:05:58.257 --> 00:05:59.591 line:0%
played by Brad Pitt,

00:05:59.591 --> 00:06:01.660 line:0%
who's cynical because he thinks
his life is meaningless,

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:03.096 line:0%
now that all the marine life
has died,

00:06:03.096 --> 00:06:04.496 line:0%
is recruited by a band of rebels

00:06:04.496 --> 00:06:06.064 line:0%
to break the last
remaining dolphin on Earth

00:06:06.064 --> 00:06:08.401 line:0%
out of a government lab
and return him to the ocean.

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:09.535 line:0%
Just as they escort him
to the edge

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:10.603 line:0%
of the water to release him,

00:06:10.603 --> 00:06:12.405 line:0%
government agents
assassinate the scientist

00:06:12.405 --> 00:06:13.839 line:0%
and, as he lays there
on the beach,

00:06:13.839 --> 00:06:16.575 line:0%
gasping his last dying breath,
the dolphin says,

00:06:16.575 --> 00:06:18.210 line:0%
"I am sorry you died
for nothing,"

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:21.080 line:0%
and the scientist said,
"I didn't die for nothing.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.482 line:0%
I found

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:24.016 line:0%
my porpoise."
[purpose]

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:26.219
-Well, I liked it.

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:28.020
[ Laughter ]
-Sea Captain?!

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.722
What are you doing back on land?

00:06:29.722 --> 00:06:32.391
-The ocean is too hot
to sail on, Seth.

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:34.493
[ Laughing ]

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:36.662
Seriously,
somebody do something.

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:38.464
[ Laughter ]
And climate scientists

00:06:38.464 --> 00:06:40.499
aren't the only ones using dire
language to warn about the

00:06:40.499 --> 00:06:42.401
real-world consequences
we're seeing right now

00:06:42.401 --> 00:06:44.737
and how little time we have
to stop climate change

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:46.772
from reaching the tipping point,
where it becomes irreversible.

00:06:46.772 --> 00:06:48.941
Yesterday,
President Biden addressed

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:51.343
the United Nations General
Assembly and said this --

00:06:51.343 --> 00:06:55.681
-This year has also brought
widespread death and devastation

00:06:55.681 --> 00:06:59.118
from the borderless
climate crisis.

00:06:59.118 --> 00:07:01.320
The extreme weather events

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.355
that we have seen
in every part of the world --

00:07:03.355 --> 00:07:05.525
and you all know it
and feel it --

00:07:05.525 --> 00:07:07.159
represent what
the secretary-general

00:07:07.159 --> 00:07:09.127
has rightly called

00:07:09.127 --> 00:07:12.898
Code Red for humanity.

00:07:12.898 --> 00:07:15.801
And the scientists and experts
are telling us

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:17.570
that we're fast approaching

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:20.907
a point of no return,
in a literal sense.

00:07:20.907 --> 00:07:22.808
-Man, usually,
when you see a guy that age

00:07:22.808 --> 00:07:25.411
use dire language like that,
it's because his adult children

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:26.879
keep forgetting
to turn the lights off

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:28.513
when they leave a room.

00:07:28.513 --> 00:07:30.382
[ As Biden ]
Come on, guys.
I'm not made of money here.

00:07:30.382 --> 00:07:31.951
This is a Code Red.

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:33.653
So the real-world effects
of climate change

00:07:33.653 --> 00:07:35.621
are very much here,
as we can see with our own eyes,

00:07:35.621 --> 00:07:38.157
and they'll keep getting worse,
unless we do something about it.

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:41.294
The good news is
we can do something about it.

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:42.661 line:0%
The pair of infrastructure bills

00:07:42.661 --> 00:07:44.430 line:0%
making their way
through Congress right now

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:45.797 line:0%
would make
significant investments

00:07:45.797 --> 00:07:48.767 line:0%
in climate infrastructure,
including a program

00:07:48.767 --> 00:07:50.269 line:0%
in the reconciliation bill
called the...

00:07:59.045 --> 00:08:00.445 line:0%
As well as strong incentives

00:08:00.445 --> 00:08:02.748 line:0%
to transition
to forms of transportation

00:08:02.748 --> 00:08:05.351 line:0%
that don't depend heavily
on fossil fuels.

00:08:05.351 --> 00:08:06.885 line:0%
-Both of those bills represent

00:08:06.885 --> 00:08:08.721 line:0%
hundreds of billions of dollars

00:08:08.721 --> 00:08:11.056 line:0%
in investments
in renewable energies,

00:08:11.056 --> 00:08:13.392 line:0%
as well as in climate
resiliency efforts

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:15.461 line:0%
to try and combat
and mitigate, really,

00:08:15.461 --> 00:08:18.130 line:0%
the damage of the effects
of climate change

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.197 line:0%
that we have been seeing

00:08:19.197 --> 00:08:21.467 line:0%
across the country
in recent weeks.

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:23.802 line:0%
-The president believes
his multitrillion-dollar

00:08:23.802 --> 00:08:26.038 line:0%
infrastructure bill
and spending package

00:08:26.038 --> 00:08:28.039 line:0%
will help the country become
more prepared

00:08:28.039 --> 00:08:29.975 line:0%
for these extreme
weather events.

00:08:29.975 --> 00:08:31.877 line:0%
Some of his climate
provisions include

00:08:31.877 --> 00:08:34.046 line:0%
tax incentives for electric cars

00:08:34.046 --> 00:08:37.316 line:0%
and plans to transition to more
renewable energy sources,

00:08:37.316 --> 00:08:39.785 line:0%
things like wind
and solar power.

00:08:39.785 --> 00:08:40.953
-That's great news.

00:08:40.953 --> 00:08:42.788
And I won't be sad
to see gas stations go,

00:08:42.788 --> 00:08:45.257
but I do think we should keep
the weird little store

00:08:45.257 --> 00:08:47.125
where they sell Slim Jims
and air fresheners

00:08:47.125 --> 00:08:48.394
and off-brand boner pills.

00:08:48.394 --> 00:08:50.396
When you're 13,
a gas station convenience store

00:08:50.396 --> 00:08:52.230
is heaven.
It's like a grocery store

00:08:52.230 --> 00:08:54.567
where all they sell you
are the stuff you like

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:55.868
and none of the stuff
that's good for you.

00:08:55.868 --> 00:08:57.669
And when you get back to the car
and your mom complains

00:08:57.669 --> 00:09:00.172
that you bought Funyuns
and Mountain Dews, you can say,

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:01.540
"Oh, I'm sorry.
They were

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:04.476
out of matcha and kale chips
at the Sunoco."

00:09:04.476 --> 00:09:06.245
[ Laughter ]
I swear, one time, I stopped

00:09:06.245 --> 00:09:07.512
at a gas station in Florida

00:09:07.512 --> 00:09:08.681
and there was a section
called...

00:09:10.082 --> 00:09:11.483
[ Laughter ]

00:09:11.483 --> 00:09:13.552
So the bills currently winding
their way through Congress

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:16.055
would invest in climate
infrastructure and clean energy.

00:09:16.055 --> 00:09:17.323
Now, traditionally,
we've been told

00:09:17.323 --> 00:09:18.424
that clean energy is, somehow,

00:09:18.424 --> 00:09:19.892
more expensive
than fossil fuels,

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:23.261
but a new study provides some
major good news on that front.

00:09:23.261 --> 00:09:25.097
It turns out it's the opposite.

00:09:25.097 --> 00:09:26.132 line:0%
-The old way of thinking

00:09:26.132 --> 00:09:28.000 line:0%
about fossil fuels being cheaper

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:30.302 line:0%
and clean energy meaning lots
of government subsidies

00:09:30.302 --> 00:09:33.272 line:0%
has now been essentially
flipped on its head.

00:09:33.272 --> 00:09:36.708 line:0%
In fact, one recent paper
out of Oxford suggests

00:09:36.708 --> 00:09:38.511 line:0%
that a rapid transition
to green energy

00:09:38.511 --> 00:09:42.615 line:0%
would save trillions of dollars,
based on energy costs, alone.

00:09:42.615 --> 00:09:44.550 line:0%
That's before you even factor in

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:46.351 line:0%
the benefits
of addressing climate change.

00:09:46.351 --> 00:09:47.587 line:0%
Quoting from the report...

00:09:57.430 --> 00:09:58.898 line:0%
If all the fossil fuel companies

00:09:58.898 --> 00:10:00.932 line:0%
stopped lobbying
against clean power,

00:10:00.932 --> 00:10:03.769 line:0%
if we let the renewable energy
trends continue

00:10:03.769 --> 00:10:06.972 line:0%
at the rate they already
are developing,

00:10:06.972 --> 00:10:10.242 line:0%
we achieve a near-net-zero
emissions energy system

00:10:10.242 --> 00:10:11.410 line:0%
within twenty-five years."

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:13.579 line:0%
Literally.
According to this report,

00:10:13.579 --> 00:10:15.547 line:0%
if we just sit back,

00:10:15.547 --> 00:10:17.550 line:0%
let things develop
at their current pace,

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:21.052 line:0%
we will reach near-net-zero
carbon emissions in 25 years.

00:10:21.052 --> 00:10:23.856
-That's right -- if we just let
clean energy develop

00:10:23.856 --> 00:10:25.391
at the rate
it's currently developing,

00:10:25.391 --> 00:10:26.792
without getting in the way,
we could reach

00:10:26.792 --> 00:10:29.128
net-zero carbon emissions
in 25 years.

00:10:29.128 --> 00:10:31.096
And, personally,
I'm in favor of that

00:10:31.096 --> 00:10:32.465
because I'd love
to take the subway

00:10:32.465 --> 00:10:34.166
without seeing pigeons
wearing snorkels.

00:10:34.166 --> 00:10:35.467
It's huge news.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:35.467 --> 00:10:37.336
The transition to clean energy
is actually cheaper

00:10:37.336 --> 00:10:39.104
and more cost-effective
than fossil fuels.

00:10:39.104 --> 00:10:40.472
We just need it
to happen faster,

00:10:40.472 --> 00:10:42.008
before we reach
the tipping point

00:10:42.008 --> 00:10:44.042
of irreversible
climate destruction,

00:10:44.042 --> 00:10:45.711
which is why we still need

00:10:45.711 --> 00:10:47.612
government subsidies
to push it along.

00:10:47.612 --> 00:10:50.149
The problem is
that the fossil fuel lobby

00:10:50.149 --> 00:10:53.519
is still doing everything it can
to lobby against clean energy

00:10:53.519 --> 00:10:55.754
and they have powerful
allies in Washington
doing their bidding,

00:10:55.754 --> 00:10:57.890
like West Virginia
Senator Joe Manchin,

00:10:57.890 --> 00:10:59.357
who chairs
the Senate Energy Committee.

00:10:59.357 --> 00:11:00.459
The New York Times
reported that...

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.268
And, not only that, Manchin...

00:11:21.379 --> 00:11:22.948 line:0%
I mean, how is it acceptable
that the guy

00:11:22.948 --> 00:11:25.851 line:0%
writing our climate policy
personally profits from coal?

00:11:25.851 --> 00:11:27.887 line:0%
It's like if,
instead of hiding his gambling,

00:11:27.887 --> 00:11:30.522 line:0%
Pete Rose called his bookie
from second base.

00:11:30.522 --> 00:11:32.057
[ As Rose ]
Yeah, I want to place a bet
against the Reds.

00:11:32.057 --> 00:11:33.058
What am I calling you from?

00:11:33.058 --> 00:11:34.460
A cellphone.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:36.662
Well, it's 1986,
so it's technically possible.

00:11:36.662 --> 00:11:38.130
[ Laughter ]
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:39.298
No, the writers Googled it.

00:11:39.298 --> 00:11:40.499
[ Laughter ]

00:11:40.499 --> 00:11:42.701
And then, of course,
there are the lunatics

00:11:42.701 --> 00:11:44.736
in the GOP and right-wing media
telling you

00:11:44.736 --> 00:11:47.940
Biden's coming to steal your
hamburgers, and outlaw cows.

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:49.808
This is why we need
sustained pressure

00:11:49.808 --> 00:11:51.276
to push Congress to implement

00:11:51.276 --> 00:11:53.678
the transformative changes
we need to stave off

00:11:53.678 --> 00:11:55.847
the worst effects of climate
change before it's too late.

00:11:55.847 --> 00:11:58.150
We're already seeing
those effects happen right now,

00:11:58.150 --> 00:11:59.351
as Bernie Sanders pointed out

00:11:59.351 --> 00:12:00.619
during a Senate speech
last month,

00:12:00.619 --> 00:12:02.855
in response to a Republican
senator from Wyoming

00:12:02.855 --> 00:12:05.057
fearmongering
about the Green New Deal.

00:12:05.057 --> 00:12:08.861 line:0%
-In case the senator
from Wyoming has missed it,

00:12:08.861 --> 00:12:11.463 line:0%
Oregon is burning.

00:12:11.463 --> 00:12:13.599 line:0%
California is burning.

00:12:13.599 --> 00:12:15.567 line:0%
Greece is burning.

00:12:15.567 --> 00:12:18.103 line:0%
There is a drought

00:12:18.103 --> 00:12:20.306 line:0%
hitting virtually every country

00:12:20.306 --> 00:12:22.541 line:0%
on Earth.

00:12:22.541 --> 00:12:24.076 line:0%
News flash.

00:12:24.076 --> 00:12:27.446 line:0%
Climate change is real!

00:12:27.446 --> 00:12:30.182 line:0%
And the United States
and other countries

00:12:30.182 --> 00:12:32.017 line:0%
have got to address it.

00:12:32.017 --> 00:12:33.986
-I love a good use of the word
news flash.

00:12:33.986 --> 00:12:36.789
For our younger viewers,
it's what people used to say

00:12:36.789 --> 00:12:38.257
before they said,
"Spoiler alert."

00:12:38.257 --> 00:12:40.125
I think it comes from,
I don't know,

00:12:40.125 --> 00:12:41.727
Chaucer? But...
[ Laughter ]

00:12:41.727 --> 00:12:43.695
...it's such an effective
old-man tactic.

00:12:43.695 --> 00:12:46.131
I love that Bernie
takes on Republicans

00:12:46.131 --> 00:12:49.201
like someone just stole his spot
in the airport parking lot.

00:12:49.201 --> 00:12:51.103
"Oh, I'm sorry,
I had a flight to catch."

00:12:51.103 --> 00:12:53.772
[ As Sanders ]
Oh, oh, I am sorry,
Your Majesty.

00:12:53.772 --> 00:12:56.241
I didn't realize you
had a flight to catch.

00:12:56.241 --> 00:12:57.810
Well, news flash.

00:12:57.810 --> 00:13:00.879
[ Laughter ]
We all have flights to catch.

00:13:00.879 --> 00:13:02.681
You think I'm here
circling the parking lot

00:13:02.681 --> 00:13:05.718
because I like buying gum
at the Hudson News?

00:13:05.718 --> 00:13:07.419
What's that, honey,
we're out of Trident?

00:13:07.419 --> 00:13:11.557
I best rush over to LaGuardia

00:13:11.557 --> 00:13:13.759
and replenish our supplies.

00:13:13.759 --> 00:13:15.694
[ Laughter ]

00:13:15.694 --> 00:13:16.995 line:0%
Climate change is here.

00:13:16.995 --> 00:13:18.997 line:0%
It's having deadly,
real-world consequences.

00:13:18.997 --> 00:13:20.398 line:0%
We need bold action now

00:13:20.398 --> 00:13:22.200 line:0%
to stave off the worst effects
before it's too late.

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:23.636 line:0%
We have an opportunity,
right now,

00:13:23.636 --> 00:13:25.437
which is why we need sustained
pressure to make it happen.

00:13:25.437 --> 00:13:27.439
And I get it --
it's easy to be distracted.

00:13:27.439 --> 00:13:28.574
A lot's going on.

00:13:28.574 --> 00:13:29.908
As Billy Joel might put it --

00:13:29.908 --> 00:13:31.309
♪ Jason's looking good
in teal ♪

00:13:31.309 --> 00:13:35.247 line:0%
-Climate change is real!

00:13:35.247 --> 00:13:36.715
-Bernie's got to learn
that cadence.

00:13:36.715 --> 00:13:38.083
[ Laughter ]

00:13:38.083 --> 00:13:39.218
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:13:39.218 --> 00:13:43.088
♪♪

00:13:43.088 --> 00:13:44.556
God's Love We Deliver
